# installer-base-amd64.pkgs — always-on core toolset, AMD64 variant.
#
# Derived from manifests/installer-base.pkgs (Sky1/arm64). Every package
# there is arch-portable EXCEPT the three called out below — see
# docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md for the full accounting. Consume the same way:
# grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)'.

# --- initramfs builder --------------------------------------------------
dracut
dracut-core

# --- DKMS accelerator rebuilds ----------------------------------------------
# gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu DROPPED — that was the arm64 cross-compiler target
# for Mali's gpu.mk invoking aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc explicitly. AMD64 has no
# equivalent CIX accelerator DKMS stack (there is no CIX GPU/NPU/VPU on this
# architecture at all — see docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md "dropped" bucket).
# Native `gcc` below is sufficient for any AMD64-native DKMS module.
dkms
build-essential
gcc
make
flex
bison
bc
libelf-dev
libselinux-dev

# --- disk / partition identify -------------------------------------------
util-linux
parted
gdisk
nvme-cli
smartmontools

# --- hardware identify ---
pciutils
usbutils
dmidecode
lshw

# --- filesystems + recovery ---
btrfs-progs
e2fsprogs
testdisk

# --- boot management ---
efibootmgr
grub-efi-amd64
grub-pc-bin
# grub-efi-amd64 REPLACES the Sky1 line's implicit rEFInd-only assumption.
# AMD64 boots GRUB, not rEFInd — see docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md and the
# operator's dual-kernel-GRUB-selection decision (MNEMOS mem_1789429924427).
# grub-pc-bios is kept too for legacy-BIOS install targets (real AMD64
# hardware still includes non-UEFI-only machines; Sky1 has no such concern).

# --- network / diag ---
dbus
dbus-broker
iwd
wireguard-tools
network-manager
netplan.io
iproute2
net-tools
iputils-ping
ethtool
tcpdump
mtr-tiny
curl
wget
rsync
firmware-realtek
firmware-linux-free
firmware-misc-nonfree

# --- operator quality-of-life ---
htop
tmux
vim
mc
tree
jq
lsof

# --- remote access ---
openssh-server
inetutils-telnetd
openbsd-inetd
busybox-static

# --- zstd (same Debian-vs-Ubuntu gap as the Sky1 manifest documents) ------
zstd

# --- NCZ kernel channels — AMD64 line -------------------------------------
# linux-image-cixmini / cixmini-boot DROPPED — Sky1-only kernel package
# names. AMD64 real package names are TBD pending the two AMD64 kernel
# builds currently in progress (v7.2.6+T2 unified stable on PROTEUS, v7.3-rc3
# edge on CERBERUS) actually landing as packaged .debs — see
# docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md. Placeholder names, confirm against the real
# built package names once available:
#   linux-image-amd64-ncz-t2      (stable, unified T2+regular)
#   linux-image-amd64-ncz-edge    (edge)

# --- locales ---------------------------------------------------------------
locales

# --- console font ---
console-setup
kbd
